Mr. Whitlatch,<br />
<br />
Attached is Marchwood's interim response to the April 20 deficiency letter,=
 covering Items 1, 2, 3, 5 and 6. The compliance manual has been rewritten =
and adopted, the code of ethics reporting log has been reconstructed for 20=
09 and 2010, both advertising pieces have been withdrawn, and the retention=
 gap has been closed with the new archiving vendor.<br />
<br />
On Item 4 we are not there yet. Marchwood's position, which counsel will se=
t out more fully, is that a fee debit executed by an unaffiliated qualified=
 custodian at the adviser's instruction is not custody by the adviser, beca=
use the adviser never holds the assets and cannot move them anywhere other =
than to its own fee account in an amount fixed by the advisory agreement.<b=
r />
<br />
I would rather resolve this on a call than in an exchange of letters. Are y=
ou and Ms. Achterberg available the week of May 30?<br />
<br />
Marguerite Vasseur-Kyle<br />
Chief Compliance Officer<br />
Marchwood Asset Management LLC
